WEBVTT

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:12.070
Wow, Mikura, even you screw up
once in a while.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.450
Pops, instead of mocking my screw-up,

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.280
why don't you think about why you've
been marked for death?

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.920
Don't you have some idea?

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.920
A connection with some occupation
in your past?

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.620
I wonder... Oh, it's Aiko!

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.380
<i>Forecaster
Aiko Hasegawa</i>

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.380
Good evening. The following is a weather
report for tomorrow.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.190
She's so fantastic! Aiko!

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.190
Tomorrow, the skies will be blue with not a
single cloud in sight but the

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:35.800
temperature will be 57 degrees.
It'll get very cold.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.570
However, if I was even a little bit late, you
would have been boned, Mikura.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.800
Tomorrow, during the daytime, the winter's
blue sky will spread throughout country.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:39.800
That guy...

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.200
The probability of rain is...

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.140
What was he, anyway

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.270
Throughout the entire day, however, it's
about three percent,

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.480
a low probability, so there should
be no need for an umbrella.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.310
What?

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.710
Now, this year, at the end of this month,

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.000
Something.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:49.710
Is that for real?

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:54.810
<i>Leo Meteor Shower Visibility Projection
North East South</i>

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:52.020
<i>Aiko Hasegawa</i>

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:51.750
What? Tell me.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.010
The Leo Meteor Shower will hit its peak.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.810
Let's quietly listen to Aiko give out the
weather report. Let's listen.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.810
From midnight to before daybreak...

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.620
While you may be a newcomer,

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:00.280
can't you read the typescript better?

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:02.080
I'm sorry.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:05.290
There are plenty of other weathercasters
who can take your place.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:09.000
You're not the only one with a
forecasting license.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.560
You're right.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.800
If I weren't around, you would've
been fired ages ago.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.790
Do you understand?

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:17.300
Yes.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.560
Oh, I'm so unlucky...

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.260
This is the weekly forecast.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.870
This week, sunshine will continue.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.800
However, the northern winds
are blowing and...

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.790
You're kidding me.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.500
This sucks.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.510
It'll rain tomorrow too.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.480
Your forecast was off.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.490
If you have a complaint,
send it to the station.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.460
My name is Leon,

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.800
the Rain Man.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.860
Leon...

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.210
Are you all right?

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.370
Please, will you give me shelter?

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.480
Please...

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:32.770
Please!

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.090
<i>Norikonda sabaibaru cousutaa</i>

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.060
The survival roller coaster we got on

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:45.830
There's no need to give up,
run by the highway

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:45.530
<i>Akirame muyoude run by the highway</i>

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.400
<i>Kimiwa inochi karagara</i>

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.600
You just barely escaped with your life

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.930
<i>Atashitachimo nodoga karakara</i>

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.200
We're thirsty

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.130
<i>Kyokugento mugendai</i>

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.340
Extremities and infinity

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.470
<i>Tomo ni sorette mugendai</i>

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:54.700
Together, they form a fantasy

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:56.370
<i>Kamaeta me hibana chiri</i>

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.570
The eyes, squaring away, are
throwing out sparks

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:59.400
<i>Oni-san kochira to shita o dasu</i>

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:59.630
"You're it! This way, " you say,
as you stick your tongue out

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:01.630
<i>Wink</i>

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:01.700
Wink

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:05.310
<i>Kyouretsuna itamini kansha</i>

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.520
Grateful for the excruciating pain

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.650
<i>Power to iu na no rei de henkan</i>

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.950
I'm restored by a gratitude
known as power

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:13.560
<i>Mou sorosoro okaeri asobareta houga
iinodewa naide shouka</i>

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:13.760
Perhaps it would be better too return soon?

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:22.460
<i>Matsugeno sukima umeruyouni aimeiku</i>

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:22.700
As though filling in the gaps between
the eyelashes, eye make

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:29.770
<i>Kokorono sukima umeruyouni I take</i>

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:29.970
As though filling in the gaps of
my heart, I take

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:34.240
<i>Gekiretsu panchide gyakuni takamaru</i>

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:34.440
On the contrary, the intensity is heightened
by a powerful punch

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:38.710
<i>Yabai shiuchi hodo yokei moechauwa</i>

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.780
The worse I'm treated, the more I get fired up

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:43.080
<i>Mouretsu panchide atashi takaburu</i>

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:43.220
I get worked up over an intense punch

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:51.510
<i>Sonna koto shite kurete arigatou</i>

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:52.060
Thank you for doing such a thing

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:54.030
<i>Sukima sukima sukimani mimai</i>

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.230
A gap, a gap, pay a sympathy visit

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.030
<i>Janai janai itainjanai?</i>

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.200
Doesn't it, doesn't it, doesn't it hurt?

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.700
<i>Mimai tsurai? ltai? Yabai?</i>

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.970
Is the visit painful? Does it hurt?
Is it dangerous?

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:02.330
<i>lkitai itai shitai, lkitai itai shitai</i>

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:02.640
I want to go, I want to stay, I want to do it

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:27.390
<i>Shell of Stars</i>

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:32.400
Letting a man you don't know nor have
ever seen before into your room...

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:34.440
You're careless.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.960
You're the one who asked for
shelter, aren't you?

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:38.630
Aren't you scared?

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.510
Of course I am.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:43.080
If you try to do something
funny to me,

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.510
I'll scream!

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.050
You already let me into your room,

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.350
so it's too late.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:50.990
I'm scared.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.690
I'm scared, but I can't believe myself.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:58.180
I can't believe I let a guy whose identity
I don't know into my room.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:19.440
What did you do to get someone
on your trail?

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.240
Even if I told you, you wouldn't believe me.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:27.250
I watch your program once in a while.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:30.490
Your speech is lousy.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:32.080
That's none of your business.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.890
But I came into this room and I understood.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:38.230
I know the reason I didn't
become uncomfortable

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.630
when I watched you being
lousy on television.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:56.820
Good morning. This is the weather for the
eastern part of the country.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:59.550
<i>Forcaster
Aiko Hasegawa</i>

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:01.660
In Tokyo, there have been eight
consecutive days of rain

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.660
Oh, Aiko. She is so cute.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.360
and there doesn't seem to be any
sign of relief in sight.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:07.800
Hey, this place. It's the nearby park?
It's blowing, it's splashing...

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:09.890
Tonight's Leo Meteor Shower, unfortunately,
won't be visible at all.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.890
Hey, are you awake?

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:11.700
By the way, Mikura,

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.800
this isn't the Drifters or some
material for a comedy group.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:15.400
This gag is old.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.960
You said you'd make the repairs immediately!

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:22.080
Does this look like a room where a
young maiden lives? Does it?

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:25.140
What was that? Something about a hairstyle?
Stay a while?

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:26.850
Pops...

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:30.150
I made some emergency repairs
but it was hopeless.

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:32.290
But hey, it was raining...

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:34.460
It's meaningless if the roof is leaking!

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.220
Completely fix it today!

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:40.600
Oh, the sounds of rain bothered me so
much, I only got eight hours of sleep!

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:44.090
Mikura, just how many hours of
sleep do you usually get?

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.100
What? Red?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.700
Something is...

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.000
Glittering?

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:57.050
I told you earlier. I'm a young maiden.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:58.170
Mr. Kurokawa! Mr. Kurokawa!

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:00.280
She's here, here!

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:02.110
Your idol's here!

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:03.680
Idol?

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:05.380
For real?!

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:11.320
Please don't move from that spot.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:17.970
She's okay.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:21.490
Please search for this man immediately.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:25.310
He's disappeared all of a sudden.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.940
The real deal, the real Aiko!

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:32.380
Excuse me, but if it's just looking for
someone, you didn't have to come to us.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:35.320
We happen to be in the business of
executing dangerous activities.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.580
Take a good look at the photograph.

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:40.150
What do you think that is?

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:43.550
Which one?

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.020
Is that it?!

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:48.350
I understood when I saw the photo.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:52.500
Why he prefers the rain,
the night and the dark.

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:54.360
Why he keeps staring into the sky.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.470
I didn't doctor the photograph!

00:07:57.470 --> 00:08:00.130
Even I still can't believe it.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:04.440
He... There's a possibility Leon isn't human.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:06.740
Are you saying that seriously?

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:09.580
Do forecasters have a habit of
having wild fantasies?

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:12.180
It doesn't matter what you think of me.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:15.550
Anyway, he was definitely being
chased by someone.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:17.890
He may be on the lam,

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:21.530
or there's a possibility he's been kidnapped,
under the worst circumstances.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:22.690
Kidnapped?

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:27.370
In other words, this is a job definitely
suited for us. We'll do it.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:29.140
You WERE listening.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:33.910
Whatever your boyfriend may be,
we'll lend out a helping hand.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:36.780
Mr. Kurokawa, you're going to
believe this person's story?

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.980
This stinks of danger.

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:41.950
So that factor alone makes it okay,
right? Right, Pops?

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:45.510
What? Oh, yeah, definitely. That's a
clever way of looking at it.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.150
Give me a laser beam gun.

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:49.110
As if such a thing exists.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.920
So, why did we come here?

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:58.790
Take a good look.

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:01.060
Who is this?

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:03.400
There's still something else?

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:04.960
Hey!

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:06.430
Right.

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:08.510
It's a Scissors macho!

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:10.880
I've got to hand it to you, ex-detective.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:12.350
So Mugi-baby,

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:14.320
I'm sort of, sort of asking you

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.150
if you might know where this rain man
in the photograph is.

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:20.610
That rain man is...

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:26.860
I'm always watching.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.690
Thank you very much.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:32.800
You get involved with him and you'll die.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:37.870
Under protection?

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.740
Yes, by his request.

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:41.910
Asking the Black Scissors for protection

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:44.310
means this is a really dangerous
matter, Mr. Kurokawa.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:48.250
Yeah, I wonder what that guy really did?

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:50.250
That rain man fellow?

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:51.550
Who cares!

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.720
That weather report lady said something
about kidnapping,

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.590
so I thought this would have a lot
more thrill to it.

00:09:57.590 --> 00:10:00.990
But there's no excitement because we
immediately found out where he is!

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:03.900
Who said I was going to tell you?

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:13.840
What?

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.400
It's me.

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:17.210
What?!

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:18.950
I'm sorry, Boss.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:20.440
We were...

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:24.750
No match for...

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.510
Closed For Today

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:29.880
I let my guard down a little and this happens.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:34.390
This is that person's...

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:37.500
That car...

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:41.230
Wait!

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:48.440
Hand it over.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:49.840
Don't know.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.800
What are you talking about?

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.510
The forecaster woman...

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:59.350
I don't want to drag her into this
but you leave me no choice.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:10:59.950
Eat this!

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:04.510
Sorry, sorry. Did I hit you too hard?

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.590
Just dangle there for a while.

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:10.230
What were you going to do to Aiko?

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:12.290
You look like a pervert!

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:13.690
Come with us.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:16.370
Who are you people?

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:17.930
The often talked about DSA.

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:19.440
DSA?

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:22.300
We were asked by Aiko to help you.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.940
Hey, Pops, shall we ignore the guy outside?

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:27.280
Leave him, leave him. He's as
good as dead, anyway.

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:28.870
He's probably a good-for-nothing.

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:30.550
What?!

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:32.640
Could he have fallen?

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:35.220
He's not around.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:37.230
Flown away?

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:40.160
That's cold. What is this? This is such a
horrible embarrassment.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:41.420
Harada, hurry, go!

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:47.640
It's been a while

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.800
since I felt the kind of pain that
make my bones rattle.

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:52.770
Don't interfere.

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:54.910
I don't want to kill you guys.

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:57.140
That line is taboo!

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.310
You wait here.

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:11.990
Mikura! What's the matter? This
isn't like you at all!

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:13.220
Get a hold of yourself!

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.450
He's not human.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:20.470
From my perspective, in a way,
you're more than human too.

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:23.160
This is no time for jokes!

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:35.620
Die.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.910
So he said. What now, Mikura?

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:39.820
You saw what he did earlier.

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:40.890
That's not possible.

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:42.160
But you saw it.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:45.390
What the hell is he? What are we
going to do, Mikura?

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.890
This course of events is known
only to the baldy.

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:50.630
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:58.200
Bingo!

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:05.210
Bulls-eye. Did that fellow die? So frail.

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.760
We've arrived so tell us.

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:25.530
What are you?

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:27.400
Why are you running away?

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:29.840
What's the deal behind that Mr. Magician?

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.610
You wouldn't believe me if I told you.

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:36.570
Whether we believe it or not is our
business. Right, Mr. Kurokawa?

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:40.950
As it is, it's too dangerous to hand
you over to Aiko so we can't.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.120
It's the rain.

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:44.240
Rain?

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.390
His target is this.

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:49.720
What is that?

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.780
What does the rain have
to do with this?

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:54.500
The rain continuing to fall right now

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.260
is intentionally controlled.

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:58.490
This can stop that rain.

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:01.700
What's he talking about?

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:02.830
Don't know.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:07.040
If I don't activate this by tonight's
Leo Meteor Shower,

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:09.480
it will continue to rain on this planet, and...

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:11.110
Tokyo...

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:13.440
No, the world will be submerged?

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:19.320
Then that means the cities will be paralyzed
and humanity will be lost.

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:21.580
Then... Then what would happen?

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:27.830
It's the same old pattern. World domination,
slam the door shut on humanity.

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:30.460
Would someone think like that, possibly?

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:33.700
Mr. Kurokawa! This guy suffers
from paranoia!

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:37.800
No, no. This man is genuinely from
outer space, correct?

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.310
See?

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:40.510
You're believing this sham story?!
See?

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:42.940
You're believing this sham story?!

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:45.580
So is that why that Mr. Magician
from earlier could...

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:48.570
Right, right. That's why he can
do tricks like that.

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:52.250
Pops, you seriously think that's so?

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:54.560
In all creation, that is to say,

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:59.930
the range of things a human being can
comprehend is this narrow, don't you think?

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:03.230
In other words, we humans are beings
who only want to believe

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:05.200
what we see in front of us as reality.

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.640
I can't do that!

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:09.630
That's too untheoretical!

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:11.010
Such a story might be possible.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.770
No, it's not!

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:17.340
I'll just show you guys my real appearance.

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:20.000
Let's have you show us!

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:29.480
Leon?

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:33.620
Don't tell Aiko.

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:36.300
If she found out, she'd...

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:38.630
We couldn't tell her anyway.

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:40.970
But she seems to realize it,

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:42.960
about you being different from humans.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:47.510
In addition, don't you think you're
misunderstanding her?

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:48.810
Misunderstanding?

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:50.500
He's still alive!

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:57.280
Hand it over.

00:15:57.590 --> 00:15:59.420
I told you I don't know.

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:03.120
With the fate of Earthlings on the line,
I will defeat you!

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:04.350
Are you serious?!

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.920
Mikura, we're probably the bad guys.

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:08.930
I don't care about the logic!

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:11.960
If I don't kick this guy's ass,
I'm not going to be satisfied!

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:13.800
You're quite right to say so.

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:15.830
What can you guys do?

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:17.260
You're quite right to say so.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:33.650
If you don't stop the bleeding in a
hurry, the woman will die.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:35.210
Aiko!

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:36.910
I have it!

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:41.020
I borrowed it a little during that
little scuffle we just had.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:44.060
I didn't even notice.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:48.130
If you have it, then that saves
me some trouble!

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:52.070
If you tell us where the weather report
girl is, I'll give it to you.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.210
There's no need for that.

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:55.870
That's what I thought.

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:02.770
Pops! I'm counting on you!

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:09.360
Harada, let's go find Aiko.

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:11.090
So after all, she's...

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.990
Most likely somewhere in that warehouse.

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:17.200
There's no other place he could have
hidden someone on short notice.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:25.700
This way.

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:33.810
Well, hand it over!

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:36.440
All right, all right, I'll pull it out!

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.280
Aiko!

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:47.520
Don't die!

00:17:48.030 --> 00:17:49.560
Harada, call an ambulance!

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:50.530
Right!

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:58.160
Leon, hurry, make this rain stop.

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:00.470
How do you know about that?

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:02.410
Mr. Magician probably told her.

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:06.670
I want to believe the man I fell
in love with...

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.380
No matter what he is...

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:11.710
Aiko...

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:15.820
Hurry, hurry and make the rain stop!

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:19.160
Do it! The Leo Meteor Shower
will soon arrive!

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.130
But I don't have it with me.

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:23.460
No, what Mikura has is...

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:25.090
Did you know?

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:28.500
On Earth, women are the strongest!

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:40.650
If you were a woman, I'd fix your corpse up

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:42.640
so you'd at least look presentable
at your funeral.

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:04.910
Mr. Kurokawa. Things like this...

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:06.130
Yeah.

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:12.340
Whoa, I might even cry.

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:54.050
It's all right now.

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:59.920
It's a stone, which doesn't exist
on this planet.

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:02.360
We'll always be together.

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:04.660
Can't I see you anymore?

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:07.840
I don't know.

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:11.540
But someday, I will definitely
come to see you.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:14.910
What's that? Where are
you going off to?

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:16.580
You're not staying here with her?

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:20.810
Instead of giving her that lame
pendant, stay here and...

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:23.610
He's from another planet so he's
got his own reasons.

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:27.690
I'll definitely, definitely come to see you.

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:32.520
The man who fell in love with me,
who loves me...

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:35.620
Don't let me be alone forever.

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:44.070
How stupid. How old are you?

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:46.670
Hey, a shooting star.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:53.540
What the...

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:55.750
Mr. Kurokawa...

00:20:55.750 --> 00:21:00.120
Harada, Mikura, let's not talk about this
incident to anyone. Don't say.

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:02.860
They wouldn't believe us anyway.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:04.320
How true.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:07.290
Oh, I'm hungry!

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:17.540
Next time, I'll kill Kurokawa.

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:24.530
But she...

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:45.670
Good morning.

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:48.540
Reporting the weather of the eastern
side of the country.

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:51.340
Tokyo is a world covered in a layer of
silver due to the snow,

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:54.170
which started to fall at daybreak.

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:55.410
Snow?!

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:59.280
It's awesome! It's this deep already!

00:21:59.850 --> 00:22:02.510
No wonder I thought it was chilly.

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:04.840
Who's that?

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:07.120
When I went shopping earlier...

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:11.330
Ms. Mikura?

00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:13.690
Someone call me?

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:16.230
Do you remember me?

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:20.600
I don't know you. Who are you?
What do you want with me?

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:24.200
Make me... Please make me your
student, Master!

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:26.340
What the hell is that?

00:22:26.340 --> 00:22:27.710
Hey, what's your name?

00:22:27.710 --> 00:22:31.240
Asami, Asami Igarashi.

00:22:31.510 --> 00:22:34.000
This school backpack midget is
from the earlier incident.

00:22:40.820 --> 00:22:44.990
Listen, young lady. We can appreciate
you going through the trouble

00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:47.430
of coming out here in this cold weather.

00:22:47.430 --> 00:22:51.900
However, we're involved in a lot of
dangerous jobs. That's why...

00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:54.030
And that was today's weather report.

00:22:54.230 --> 00:22:59.570
Now, everyone in the DSA, did
you see today's broadcast?

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:06.910
<i>Forecaster
Aiko Hasegawa</i>

00:23:00.110 --> 00:23:02.980
Allow me to say a word of thanks.

00:23:03.880 --> 00:23:06.910
Thank you. I'm feeling very well.

